From d4f688cbf885551da208193cb7c46ba80c09f24e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jackwang0009 <93422958+jackwang0009@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:47:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [upstream-candidate] Write inline images back as inline
 images

CPDF_PageContentGenerator::ProcessImage() returned early for inline
images, so every BI ... ID ... EI object disappeared as soon as its
content stream was regenerated.

Write them back in place: `q <graphics state> <matrix> cm BI <dict> ID
<data> EI Q`. The dictionary is written from the image stream's
dictionary with the abbreviated keys, color space names and filter names
of ISO 32000-1 tables 93 and 94 (the parser expands them), minus the
/Length, /Subtype and /Type entries the parser adds. The data is the raw
stream data, still encoded with whatever filters the dictionary names,
so nothing is decoded or re-encoded. The dictionary is serialized before
anything is emitted; a value that cannot be expressed inline (a stream
or an indirect reference) drops the object without leaving an open `q`.

A color space that an inline image selects by resource name is replaced
by the resource object when the image is parsed. CPDF_Image now keeps
that name and object for inline images, and the generator writes the
name again when the holder's /ColorSpace resources still map it to the
same object, or realizes the object as a new FXC resource otherwise
(for instance when the object was moved to another page). Device color
spaces and Indexed spaces over a device base with a string lookup stay
inline.

CPDF_Image::SetImage()/SetJpegImage()/SetJpegImageInline() replace the
stream, so the image stops being an inline image and is written as an
XObject, as before.

Tests: CPDFPageContentGeneratorTest.ProcessInlineImage (ASCIIHex gray,
raw RGB whose data contains "EI ", image mask, named Indexed resource,
filter chain with /DecodeParms, inline Indexed; generate -> parse ->
generate is stable), ProcessInlineImageOnAnotherPage and
ProcessInlineImageWithNewBitmap. pdfium_unittests and
pdfium_embeddertests: no new failures.

Verification (ops_diff.py): missing inline-image events 6 -> 0 on the
synthetic corpus (struct-inline-image.pdf); no-diff pages 54/67 -> 55/67
synthetic, 384/388 -> 384/388 public.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
